WEBVTT

00:00:04.721 --> 00:00:07.853
The first time you open Mamoru, you create a passkey.

00:00:08.471 --> 00:00:11.575
It lives on your device, and opens with your face,

00:00:11.575 --> 00:00:13.934
your fingerprint, or your screen lock.

00:00:13.934 --> 00:00:15.673
No password, no seed phrase.

00:00:16.354 --> 00:00:20.006
Once you have an account, you use it to prove it's you, and to sign.

00:00:22.721 --> 00:00:24.638
Your passkey signs permissions.

00:00:24.638 --> 00:00:28.903
With one signature, you let Mamoru move your funds, within set rules.

00:00:29.471 --> 00:00:31.350
Mamoru doesn't ask for every move.

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:34.609
If a relevant condition changes, it asks you to sign again.

00:00:35.471 --> 00:00:38.850
And taking money out always needs your passkey. Only you can.

00:00:42.238 --> 00:00:45.520
If you lose your passkey, there is no way to recover your account.

00:00:46.354 --> 00:00:49.003
So back it up as soon as you create your account.

00:00:49.003 --> 00:00:51.328
It syncs with your Apple or Google account,

00:00:51.328 --> 00:00:53.815
and on a new phone, it opens the same account.

00:00:54.604 --> 00:00:57.602
Keep your passkey safe, and you can always get your money back.
